<title>TURKEY: Turkey expects $3.5 bln from '97 Telekom sell-off.</title>
<headline>Turkey expects $3.5 bln from '97 Telekom sell-off.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey expects to raise $3.5 billion from the privatisation of Turkish Telekom and another $1 billion from sale of licences for Global System for Mobile Communication (GSM), Erdogan Oner, budget director of the Finance Ministry told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We aim a revenue of $3.5 billion from the privatisation of Turk Telekom and $1 billion from GSM licences,&quot; Oner said following Finance Minister Abdullatif Sener's press conference to unveil Turkey's 1997 budget draft and economic targets.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
